=== real root cause (confirmed via cilium-dbg endpoint policy JSON) ===
Both the plain K8s NetworkPolicy 'allow-frontend-to-backend' (no L7 restriction) and the
CiliumNetworkPolicy 'l7-http-backend' (L7-restricted) simultaneously grant frontend->backend
ingress. Cilium's policy model is most-permissive-wins across overlapping selectors for the
same L4 port, so the unrestricted plain NetworkPolicy's l7-rules:null silently overrode the
CiliumNetworkPolicy's L7 restriction. Fixed by deleting the redundant plain NetworkPolicy so
ONLY the CiliumNetworkPolicy governs this specific traffic.
networkpolicy.networking.k8s.io "allow-frontend-to-backend" deleted from default namespace
